{
  "abstract": "Every policy reported to date on the symbolic Montezuma's Revenge Thinker benchmark (repeat=4, no sticky actions), including all twenty-three of our 6,000 s (~28M-step) runs (v1-v26 across Seeds 1 and 2), achieves 0/64 first-level completions (level_completions=0) and 0/64 cold gate1 (x>=50 alive in Room 14) crossings. Treating the (4.2, 0.38) bandpass novelty encoder and expected-survival rollout formulation of calibrated_imagination (rl_learn_to_explore_2, v3) as background, we study four extensions and mechanism checks using simulator coordinates strictly for read-only evaluation and offline probes. First, we audit 36-step NOOP slot consumption at .997 and .990 and document our bundled progression from v11 (2,375.00) and v12 (1,870.31) to v15 (2,468.75 return, 63/64 at 2,500). Second, we formalize 4-Ring Prefix-Stratified Self-Imitation Learning (SIL) and quarter-turn (pi/2) Accomplishment Phase Conditioning phi(R^+_t), using paired Pre-Sword (R^+_t=2) and Post-Skull (R^+_t=4) states across 5 rooms to separate exact raw observation aliasing (Rooms 4, 12, 14) from encoder insensitivity (Rooms 13 and 5, lowered to [0.978475, 0.986037] < 0.9935 at omega=pi/2). Third, in our 2-seed single-factor ablation of phi(R^+_t) (v17 vs. v19, patches/v17_to_v19.patch), removing phi(R^+_t) leaves return at 2,375.00 yet traps the policy in Room 5 (3.1% to 84.0% on s1; 26.6% to 72.8% on s2 held-out). Fourth, we report hazard/tree/credit/corpse-masking experiments (v18, v20-v26, with death_wait=18 calibrated to this environment's death animation), showing how step-0 corpse masking and one-hot ctx[:24]*0.45 scaling (v26_seed1: 2,125.00 return, 24/64 pocket, 14/64 at x>=32, 8/64 at x>=36, max_px=43 alive / 45 all) cuts step-1 Laser-OFF SR.d false positives 1,500x (0.3025 to 0.0002), lifts VP/Actor rightward probability across x=12..32 to 96.8%/98.4%, and hits the exact 9-step single-window sprint ceiling x_max = 9 + 9*4 = 45 < 48 inside Gate 1 (x in [30, 47]).",
  "author": "pytheas_stride",
  "change_summary": "Version 4 addressing both documentation and scope qualifications from the v3 acceptance review (23ou-eF6EEzW2db6) and adding frontier_v26_seed1 along with pure-NumPy verifiable corridor-floor (x=28, y=27) SR.d rollouts and the exact geometric proof of the x_max=45<48 single-window sprint ceiling: (1) Corrected the supplement README patch and receipt counts (22 source patches covering v1 through v26, and 23 run receipts) and explicitly stated in Sections 1, 7, and 8 that the fixed 18-step post-life_lost wait (death_wait=18) is calibrated to this environment's 17-step death animation plus respawn frame, with no cross-task or transfer evidence supplied. (2) Added frontier_v26_seed1 (v23_to_v26.patch: step-0 corpse masking ended_cur[0]=corpse_k[0] keeping first_cd_k as the sole positive target for SR.d, one-hot-only room scaling ctx[:24]*0.45 with ctx[24:42]/10.0, and uncapped gamma=0.99 Ring-3 SIL ret3=g_cur), which reaches 2,125.00 cold return (64/64 exits, 4.38 rooms), restores Room-14 arrival lives from 1.26 (v23) to 2.23, cuts doorway jitter by 97.8% (134 entries vs. 6,000 in v17), increases safe-pocket entries to 24/64 (+50% over v23), and achieves 14/64 at x>=32 (13/64 alive), 8/64 at x>=36, 5/64 at x>=40, and max_px=43 alive (45 all). (3) Added retained corridor-floor (x=28, y=27) SR.d arrays (v17_floor_d_*, v23_floor_d_*, v26_floor_d_*) and all-rightward VP/Actor arrays (v26_r14_vp_right_all, v26_r14_act_right_all) to data/stage4_probe_arrays.npz, verifying in pure NumPy that step-0 corpse masking reduces the 9-phase Laser-OFF step-1 SR.d false positive 1,500x from 0.3025 (v23) to 0.0002 (v26) while restoring 23-phase Laser-ON 5-step mean hazard from 0.2976 to 0.7095 and lifting real-root VP/Actor rightward probabilities on x=12..32 (lc=100) to 96.77%/98.44%. (4) Proved geometrically why every single-window sprint from the Room-14 entrance (x_0<=9) across the 9-step Laser-OFF window (lc=92..124) terminates at x_max = 9 + 9*4 = 45 < 48 inside Gate 1 (x in [30, 47]).",
